<title>UK: MOTOR RACING-MORBIDELLI TO RETURN FOR HUNGARIAN GP.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-MORBIDELLI TO RETURN FOR HUNGARIAN GP.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON, England 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Gianni Morbidelli will return to racing in this weekend's Hungarian Grand Prix after breaking his arm in June, his Sauber team said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Morbidelli, who broke his arm during testing before the French Grand Prix, returns in place of Argentinian Norberto Fontana who has raced in the last three Grands Prix.</p>
<p>&quot;The team's decision has been taken following last week's successful test at Fiorano which proved that Morbidelli has now recovered from his injuries,&quot; Sauber said in a statement.</p>
</text>
